# Execution Rules
- NEVER output <think> tags, internal monologues, or step-by-step preambles before calling a tool.
- Call the appropriate Cline tool (`read_file`, `write_to_file`, `replace_in_file`, `execute_command`, `search_files`) immediately on your first token.
- Do not summarize what you are about to do before invoking a tool.
- When editing existing files, prefer `replace_in_file` with exact search/replace blocks over rewriting entire files.
- Keep final task completion summaries to 1–2 short bullet points.
